=== Summary
tag::overview[]

At this point, you can do all the basic local Git operations—creating or cloning a repository, making changes, staging and committing those changes, and viewing the history of all the decisions your project has been through. You’ve even tagged your first major milestone: `v0.1-concept`.

Next, we’ll cover Git’s killer feature: its branching model. This is where Nora and Sam truly unlock the power of parallel exploration.
